ite_8291: raise the keyboard brightness ceiling from 50 to 100

The ITE 8291 (048d:600b) in the XMG APEX 16 MAX keeps getting brighter up to a
brightness byte of 100 (0x64); tuxedo-drivers clamps at 0x32. Verified by hand with
raw "09 02 <value>" feature reports (contrib/ite8291-raw-brightness.py): 10 < 50 < 100,
255 is not brighter than 100. This constant also sets multi_max_intensity, so colors
get the same 0..100 range. Machine-specific build; not meant for upstream as-is.

--- a/src/ite_8291/ite_8291.c
+++ b/src/ite_8291/ite_8291.c
@@ -104,7 +104,8 @@
 
 // led_classdev names, default and max brightness
 //#define ITE8291_KBD_BRIGHTNESS_MAX	0xff
-#define ITE8291_KBD_BRIGHTNESS_MAX	0x32
+// 0x32 upstream; the XMG APEX 16 MAX keyboard is visibly brighter up to 0x64.
+#define ITE8291_KBD_BRIGHTNESS_MAX	0x64
 #define ITE8291_KBD_BRIGHTNESS_DEFAULT	0x00
 
 #define ITE8291_KB_COLOR_DEFAULT_RED	0xff
